+/// A module that reaches itself through an import is a clean error, not a hang.
+///
+/// The bytecode loader recorded the module as loaded *before* running it, so a
+/// self-import would have recursed through `compile_module` until the stack ran
+/// out. A caught error is the contract: the failure is reachable from the
+/// program rather than fatal.
+#[test]
+fn edge_a_circular_import_is_a_caught_error_not_a_hang() {
